// A closure ARRAY handed back by an un-annotated inferred return and bound at MODULE scope.
// `vl check` returned 0 and the module failed to validate: the global's cell was typed `i32`
// while the element read wants `(ref null $type)`.
//
// `globalKind`'s ref-array rung (`exprRefArray`) resolves the element only from a return
// ANNOTATION, so the un-annotated one fell to its `i32` guess. The arena records the array
// type either way. The three ingredients are module scope, the un-annotated inferred return,
// and the element being read — the identical program inside a function ran, so did the
// annotated return, and so did every other element rep (struct, string, i32, f64).
// See D1625. Should print 55.
function deliver() { return [(n: i32) => n + 1] }
const v = deliver()
const g = (m: i32) => v[0](m)
print(g(54))
